# How to cite the RPI Thesis Toolkit itself (not RPI's requirements or anyone's
# thesis). Maintainers: "version" and "date-released" describe the latest
# published release (see docs/project/maintenance.md, "Make a release").
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this toolkit, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "RPI Thesis Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  An unofficial, community-made LaTeX starter and plain-language guide for
  graduate theses and dissertations (master's, PhD, and DEng) at Rensselaer
  Polytechnic Institute (RPI). It is not affiliated with or endorsed by RPI or
  its Office of Graduate Education, and it includes no RPI-owned materials.
authors:
  - given-names: Diyanko
    family-names: Bhowmik
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/diyanko/rpi-thesis-toolkit"
url: "https://diyanko.github.io/rpi-thesis-toolkit"
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - thesis
  - dissertation
  - template
  - Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute
